<GuideLayout
  title="Privacy policy of this Canadian salary calculator 2026"
  description="How Canada Net Pay handles your data. No personal salary or financial data is collected, stored, or transmitted. All calculations run in your browser."
  publishDate="2026-06-27"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <p><em>Last updated: October 4, 2026</em></p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>
    Canada Net Pay is a static website. All calculations run entirely in your browser.
    We do not collect, store, or transmit any salary or personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Collection</h2>
  <p><strong>The calculator collects nothing.</strong> Specifically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>No salary, income, or financial information is sent to any server.</li>
    <li>No account registration is required.</li>
    <li>No advertising cookies are used.</li>
    <li>No personal information is sold to third parties.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the Calculator Works</h2>
  <p>All tax calculations are performed client-side in your web browser using JavaScript. The numbers you enter never leave your device. When you share a URL with calculator parameters (e.g., salary amount and province), that information is encoded in the URL hash fragment, which is not sent to our servers. If someone opens such a link, the page address, including those parameters, is part of what our audience measurement records (see below).</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>Microsoft Clarity shows us how visitors move through the salary and tax pages: which links get clicked, how far each page is scrolled, which pages are opened (with their address), the device and browser in use, and a rough location inferred from the IP address. Salary, province or pay-frequency values typed into the calculator are masked in the browser before anything leaves it. Microsoft Clarity sets the cookies <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day), and Microsoft may set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains.</p>
  <p>Nothing asks for your agreement first: Clarity starts with the page, and canadanetpay.com displays neither a notice nor a consent banner. You can keep it out by blocking clarity.ms or third-party cookies in your browser settings, then clearing this site's stored data to delete any cookie already written; net pay, CPP and EI results are computed the same way without it. Microsoft keeps session recordings 30 days and aggregated statistics up to 13 months. Microsoft may process this data outside Canada, including in the United States; its handling is described in its <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy statement</a>.</p>
  <p>We also use Google Analytics 4, provided by Google Ireland Limited (Google LLC for transfers), which loads the same way when the page opens, with no notice and no consent banner. It records the pages viewed, where the visit came from, visit duration and engagement, device type and browser, and an approximate location (country, city) derived from the IP address, which Google Analytics 4 does not store. The purpose is audience measurement, on the basis of our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used. Google Analytics 4 sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> (2 years) and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code> (2 years). The data is kept for 14 months (set on our property) and is transferred to Google LLC in the United States, which is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. To refuse it, block third-party cookies or the domain google-analytics.com in your browser, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">official Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>; the calculator works without it.</p>

  <h2>Local Storage</h2>
  <p>The website uses your browser’s local storage to save your theme preference (light/dark mode). This data stays on your device and is not transmitted anywhere.</p>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>The website is hosted on static hosting infrastructure. Apart from Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics 4 (Google Ireland Limited, Google LLC), described above, we do not use third-party advertising, tracking pixels, or social media widgets that could collect your data.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes, for instance because a measurement tool is added or removed, the new
    text replaces this one and the "Last updated" date at the top moves forward.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this privacy policy, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
  </p>
